    <node id="吴国">
      <data key="d0">吴国</data>
      <data key="d1">地点</data>
      <data key="d2">吴国 was a historical state in ancient China, most prominently known for its prolonged and intense rivalry with the neighboring state of Yue (越国). This antagonistic relationship is a central theme in its history, with the two states being described as mutual enemies.

The kingdom was ruled by kings, most famously King Fuchai (吴王夫差). It possessed notable military resources, including skilled swordsmen (吴国剑士) and valuable natural resources such as fine tin (良锡). Ultimately, the state of Wu was defeated and conquered by its rival, Yue.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8a415d6907f0cafb86835c412854f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3e318eb3b9f5e9c1bd450e13ff5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f20b87683fe0cc8608a321ff18feb71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8283a4a379ab2b74495b2a64a83b7b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939cc8f0980bb7b81255939246f7fe66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76f36e0abe52b904e30fbb2a78b9a4a4</data>
