    <node id="范蠡">
      <data key="d0">范蠡</data>
      <data key="d1">人物</data>
      <data key="d2">范蠡 is a prominent historical figure who served as a high-ranking official (大夫 or 大臣) in the state of Yue during the Spring and Autumn period. He is best known for his role as a key advisor and strategist to King Goujian of Yue, assisting him in the prolonged struggle and eventual conquest of the rival state of Wu. This political service is consistently highlighted across the provided descriptions.

Beyond his statecraft, the descriptions detail several other facets of his life and activities. He is noted for his involvement in military and martial affairs, including a conflict with swordsmen from Wu and his own slight proficiency in swordsmanship. He actively sought to strengthen Yue's military, notably by recommending the swordsmith Xue Zhu and attempting to recruit the hermit A Qing to train Yue's soldiers. His personal life is also referenced, particularly his romantic relationship with the famous beauty Xi Shi, with whom he was reunited after the fall of Wu. The descriptions also mention his origin as a native of the state of Chu and his act of taking in A Qing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8a415d6907f0cafb86835c412854f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3e318eb3b9f5e9c1bd450e13ff5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f20b87683fe0cc8608a321ff18feb71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8283a4a379ab2b74495b2a64a83b7b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939cc8f0980bb7b81255939246f7fe66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93cef7b7f368309937f9f274b9ad084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013870c1938481d1558d4c2e439c83d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76f36e0abe52b904e30fbb2a78b9a4a4</data>
