    <node id="越国">
      <data key="d0">越国</data>
      <data key="d1">地点</data>
      <data key="d2">越国 was a historical state in ancient China, most prominently associated with King Goujian. It is consistently described as a country ruled by Goujian, who is a central figure in its history. The state is noted for its adversarial relationship with the rival state of Wu, with which it was in conflict.

The kingdom was also home to several key historical figures. Notably, the advisors Fan Li and Wen Zhong are identified as belonging to or serving the state of Yue. Fan Li is specifically mentioned as being from Yue, and he, along with Wen Zhong, played crucial roles in the state's affairs. Furthermore, there is a reference to the state's plans related to sword-casting, indicating an interest in metallurgy or military preparation.

In summary, Yue (越国) was an ancient Chinese state defined by the rule of King Goujian, its prolonged conflict with the state of Wu, and the service of renowned advisors like Fan Li and Wen Zhong. Its history encompasses both political-military struggles and cultural or technological endeavors such as sword-casting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8a415d6907f0cafb86835c412854f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f20b87683fe0cc8608a321ff18feb71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8283a4a379ab2b74495b2a64a83b7b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939cc8f0980bb7b81255939246f7fe66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76f36e0abe52b904e30fbb2a78b9a4a4</data>
