    <node id="林玉龙">
      <data key="d0">林玉龙</data>
      <data key="d1">人物</data>
      <data key="d2">林玉龙 is a character who is consistently identified as the husband of 任飞燕. He is depicted as a strong, burly man and a skilled practitioner of the single-blade (单刀) weapon. His relationship with his wife is marked by frequent arguments and conflict, including instances where they chase each other or are involved in disputes with other characters.

A significant portion of his narrative involves interactions with other figures in the story. He is described as pursuing 萧中慧 and later engaging in combat with 卓天雄, during which he is immobilized through acupoint striking (点穴). He is also noted for being struck by 袁冠南. Despite these conflicts, he and his wife are associated with the "夫妻刀法" (Husband and Wife Blade Technique). He is portrayed as someone who teaches or guides others, including 袁冠南, in this blade technique, though it is noted that he and 任飞燕 themselves do not perform it well together.

In summary, 林玉龙 is a martial artist and the husband of 任飞燕, characterized by his use of a single blade, his volatile relationship with his wife, and his involvement in various confrontations and martial arts instruction within the story.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4113f95e5f082a0315358bdf5af6637c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f95ffedda6d4385d0635ab387fd33e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3394ed148cdddca4307d9824a1c13c0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f620491f0a1c7878e2dae198a3326f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f6b35d7c1b17ad3c17434ffbeb5dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1335384b66ee37afc8701e4820a3e980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e39d6adc7a5461089ad8d5d04a3b77b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aebe992daba05e1d9f12616214d70c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d459cf4cb883a4446fd05607fa4651f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed3d0128804d3e005420d33a6d13ce3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca2e56bea8c78422f652b26f5a438fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20d894e54878536e4af6d96c9a33bced&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc62bee742fe92b0a19092eb807898f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5003b73156eb85d8a9f59ea76f1d5d4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19b2a43f08ffa1730c1ff0587e2ac18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7761ca8ce14dfd94808e217ac5f8fec3</data>
